[ti:Built This From A Dream]
[00:05.72][Intro]
[00:05.80]Blue light's the only thing still awake in here
[00:11.68]Everyone else went home hours ago, it's clear
[00:16.96]I keep staring at the same broken little piece
[00:23.32]Telling myself just one more try before I sleep
[00:33.28][Verse]
[00:33.36]Started this thing back when the leaves were green
[00:35.84]Now there's frost outside and I'm still stuck between
[00:39.00]What I pictured and this half-built, stubborn machine
[00:42.20]That only works when nobody else can see
[00:44.88]Every time I fix one thing, something else gives out
[00:48.36]But I've learned to love the problem, not the doubt
[00:51.24]My friends ask when it's done, I just laugh and say
[00:54.92]It's ready when it's ready, not a day
[00:57.80]So I sit with the mess until it makes sense
[01:01.32]Trade my weekends for a little more evidence
[01:04.60]That the thing I see isn't just in my head
[01:08.28]One more late night, one more thread
[01:11.96](Piece by piece - piece by piece - watch it grow)
[01:15.28](Break it down - break it down - then I know)
[01:18.56](Start again - start again - till it's clean)
[01:21.64](I built this - built this - from a dream)
[01:37.80][Verse]
[01:37.88]I've rebuilt the same idea a dozen times
[01:40.76]Thrown out the parts that only looked good on paper lines
[01:43.84]Nobody claps when something quietly works right
[01:47.08]But I felt that click at two in the morning light
[01:50.40]My family thinks I'm just staring at a screen
[01:53.68]They don't see the little world I'm trying to build between
[01:56.96]The failures, and the one time that it holds
[02:00.88]That's the part of me that nobody's told
[02:03.56]So I sit with the mess until it makes sense
[02:07.04]Trade my weekends for a little more evidence
[02:10.32]That the thing I see isn't just in my head
[02:14.04]One more late night, one more thread
[02:17.84][Drop]
[02:17.92](Piece by piece - piece by piece - watch it grow)
[02:21.00](Break it down - break it down - then I know)
[02:24.28](Start again - start again - till it's clean)
[02:27.36](I built this - built this - from a dream)
[02:31.48]Maybe it takes a year to make one thing feel true
[02:37.84]Maybe that's the cost of building something new
[02:43.36]But when it finally runs the way I always dreamed
[02:50.12]Every quiet hour will have meant exactly what it seemed
[02:57.16][Final Drop]
[02:57.24](Piece by piece - piece by piece - watch it grow)
[03:00.36](Break it down - break it down - then I know)
[03:03.64](Start again - start again - till it's clean)
[03:06.68](I built this - built this - from a dream)
[03:19.76](It finally works, and it was worth it)
[03:32.84](It finally works, and it was worth it)
